 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Closed Loop on Face:** If the surface intersects a grid face in a closed curve lying completely within that face, special handling is required. Both adjacent cubes must be parametrizable in the direction perpendicular to the face. The "bubble" must not leave the cube on the opposite face, as this would require the gradient to change more than $\pi/2$. The bubble is continuously flattened towards the face by linear interpolation and pushed through to remove the intersection loop [S1].
